{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-7810] :obs/product [:product/id :product/bullhorn] :obs/price-summary "No public pricing; sales-gated custom quote, no free trial; third-party benchmarks estimate Starter $99/user/mo (1-2 users), Core $165/user/mo, Pro custom; annual contracts commonly start near $20k/yr for small teams once implementation fees ($1k-50k+) and ~20% renewal increases are included" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/estimated :obs/source-url "https://www.pin.com/blog/bullhorn-pricing/" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260716-03" :obs/at "2026-07-16" :obs/seq 129}
{:rec/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-7810] :rec/band-low 60000.0 :rec/band-high 150000.0 :rec/unit "¥/agency/月 (flat, unlimited seats)" :rec/rationale "All 4 surveyed competitors price per-recruiter-seat ($25-315/user/mo), so cost scales with headcount; a typical 3-5-staff community agency's real spend lands ~¥22k-90k/月 (Zoho Professional) up to ~¥74k-89k/月 (Bullhorn Core / Crelate's 5-seat floor) at ~¥150/$. Cloud-itonami's flat, unlimited-seat model removes the per-seat penalty as an agency grows and is priced to undercut per-seat totals past ~4-5 staff, while the top of the band reflects the governed audit ledger + hard work-authorization/visa-consent check (入管法/I-9/right-to-work/AufenthG §4a) none of the 4 competitors enforce as an ungoverned block. This also lands in the same ¥50k-150k/月 range independently validated for the sibling flagships (isic-6399, isic-6310), giving the portfolio a consistent managed-tenant price point across all three." :rec/run-id "pricing-intel-20260716-03" :rec/at "2026-07-16" :rec/seq 130}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-5820] :obs/product [:product/id :product/salesforce-sales-cloud] :obs/price-summary "Published list (vendor pricing page; direct fetch returned 403 on 2026-07-17, list prices cross-verified same day via MarketBetter/PulseSignal aggregators): Starter Suite $25, Pro Suite $100, Enterprise $175, Unlimited $350, Agentforce 1 Sales $550 /user/mo — all per-user, annual billing except Starter; ~6% Enterprise/Unlimited uplift Aug 2025" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/published :obs/source-url "https://www.salesforce.com/sales/pricing/" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260717-01" :obs/at "2026-07-17" :obs/seq 131}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-5820] :obs/product [:product/id :product/hubspot-sales-hub] :obs/price-summary "Vendor pricing page (fetched directly 2026-07-17): Free $0 (up to 2 users); Starter from $7/mo/seat billed annually ($20 monthly); Professional from $90/mo/seat annually ($100 monthly) + one-time $1,500 onboarding fee; Enterprise from $150/mo/seat + one-time $3,500 onboarding fee — per-seat throughout" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/published :obs/source-url "https://www.hubspot.com/pricing/sales" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260717-01" :obs/at "2026-07-17" :obs/seq 132}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-5820] :obs/product [:product/id :product/pipedrive] :obs/price-summary "Published list (vendor pricing page 403 on direct fetch 2026-07-17; verified via emailtooltester/Forbes Advisor aggregators): Lite $14, Growth $39, Premium $59, Ultimate $79 /seat/mo billed annually ($24/$49/$79/$99 monthly) — per-seat; plan names renamed from Essential/Advanced/Professional/Power" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/published :obs/source-url "https://www.pipedrive.com/en/pricing" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260717-01" :obs/at "2026-07-17" :obs/seq 133}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-5820] :obs/product [:product/id :product/zoho-crm] :obs/price-summary "Vendor pricing page (fetched directly 2026-07-17, geo-localized INR display): Standard INR 800, Professional INR 1,400, Enterprise INR 2,400, Ultimate INR 2,600 /user/mo (annual saves up to 34%); USD list cross-checked via aggregators: $14/$23/$40/$52 /user/mo billed annually — per-seat" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/published :obs/source-url "https://www.zoho.com/crm/zohocrm-pricing.html" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260717-01" :obs/at "2026-07-17" :obs/seq 134}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-5820] :obs/product [:product/id :product/dynamics-365-sales] :obs/price-summary "Vendor pricing page (fetched directly 2026-07-17): Sales Professional $65.00, Sales Enterprise $105.00, Sales Premium $150.00 /user/mo paid yearly; Microsoft Relationship Sales variable-priced with 10-seat minimum — per-seat" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/published :obs/source-url "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics-365/products/sales/pricing" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260717-01" :obs/at "2026-07-17" :obs/seq 135}
{:rec/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-5820] :rec/band-low 50000.0 :rec/band-high 150000.0 :rec/unit "\u00a5/org/\u6708 (flat, unlimited seats)" :rec/rationale "All 5 surveyed competitors price per-seat ($14-550/user/mo), so a growing sales team pays linearly per rep; a typical 5-rep SMB team's real spend at ~\u00a5150/$ spans ~\u00a517k/\u6708 (Zoho Professional) through ~\u00a544k (Pipedrive Premium), ~\u00a568k+onboarding (HubSpot Professional), ~\u00a579k (Dynamics 365 Sales Enterprise), up to ~\u00a5131k (Salesforce Enterprise). Cloud-itonami's flat unlimited-seat managed tenant removes the per-seat penalty past ~4-5 reps, and the top of the band reflects the governed layer none of the 5 ship as a structural block (discount-authority limits, subscription-entitlement scope, pipeline stage-sequence validity, ASC 606/IFRS 15 straight-line revrec recompute, all behind an independent SubscriptionGovernor with an append-only audit ledger \u2014 competitors offer at most configurable approval workflows). Lands in the same \u00a550k-150k/\u6708 managed-tenant range independently validated for isic-6399/6310/7810, keeping one consistent portfolio price point; Managed CRM (Starter) opened at \u00a580,000/\u6708 flat per ADR-2607161745 convention." :rec/run-id "pricing-intel-20260717-01" :rec/at "2026-07-17" :rec/seq 136}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-851] :obs/product [:product/id :product/schoolcues] :obs/price-summary "Small/private-school all-in-one management platform (admissions, SIS, gradebook, communications, payments): vendor's own published pricing starts at $75/mo base for a 12-month school year, plus up to $1/mo per student for additional modules -- direct fetch of schoolcues.com blocked by the site's own bot-protection (403), so this figure is captured via search-engine synthesis of the vendor's own public blog content, not independently re-verified against a live page render" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/estimated :obs/source-url "https://www.schoolcues.com/blog/the-small-schools-sis-demystifying-cost-and-maximizing-your-return/" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260722-01" :obs/at "2026-07-22" :obs/seq 137}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-851] :obs/product [:product/id :product/bloomz] :obs/price-summary "K-12 parent-communication/wellbeing platform: schoolwide pricing is published at $3/student/year, price-locked for the contract term, free for parents -- confirmed directly on Bloomz's own comparison blog (not a third-party estimate)" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/published :obs/source-url "https://www.bloomz.com/blog/best-parentsquare-alternatives-2026/" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260722-01" :obs/at "2026-07-22" :obs/seq 138}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-851] :obs/product [:product/id :product/parentsquare] :obs/price-summary "K-12 parent-communication platform: no published price table anywhere -- every package routes to a sales conversation, independently confirmed across 3 sources (G2 alternatives listing, an independent ParentSquare-alternatives comparison article, and Bloomz's own competitor comparison). An earlier search pass surfaced an unverified \"$3,600/year for up to 600 students\" figure from aggregated search synthesis; two follow-up direct fetches of comparison pages that should have contained it did NOT reproduce that number, so it is deliberately NOT recorded here as an observation to avoid propagating an unconfirmed figure" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/opaque :obs/source-url "https://www.g2.com/products/parentsquare/competitors/alternatives" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260722-01" :obs/at "2026-07-22" :obs/seq 139}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-851] :obs/product [:product/id :product/brightwheel] :obs/price-summary "Early-education/childcare management platform: no published price table -- pricing page is a \"Request pricing\" lead-gen form asking for role, max enrollment capacity, number of locations and launch timing" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/opaque :obs/source-url "https://info.mybrightwheel.com/compare-brightwheel-vs-parentsquare" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260722-01" :obs/at "2026-07-22" :obs/seq 140}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-851] :obs/product [:product/id :product/procare] :obs/price-summary "Childcare-business management platform: pricing URL redirects to a request-a-quote page; markets \"everything needed... for one low monthly price\" without ever disclosing the number" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/opaque :obs/source-url "https://bloomily.app/blog/procare-vs-brightwheel-comparison" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260722-01" :obs/at "2026-07-22" :obs/seq 141}
{:rec/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-851] :rec/band-low 15000.0 :rec/band-high 40000.0 :rec/unit "¥/school/月 (flat, unlimited seats)" :rec/rationale "Only 2 of 5 surveyed competitors publish real numbers (SchoolCues, Bloomz); the other 3 (ParentSquare, Brightwheel, Procare) are sales-gated with zero public pricing -- a starker opacity pattern than 6399/6310/7810/5820 saw. Converting the 2 published anchors at ~¥150/$ for an illustrative 300-student primary school: Bloomz's $3/student/year lands at ~¥11,000/月; SchoolCues' $75/mo base + $1/mo/student lands at ~¥56,000/月 at full modular buildout. The ¥15k-40k/月 band sits inside that real range, biased toward the low-to-mid end because isic-851 is COORDINATION-ONLY (attendance/scheduling/supply/staffing/safety-flag proposals + audit ledger) -- deliberately narrower than either comp's full suite (no parent broadcast messaging, no tuition/payment processing, no gradebook/SIS). Unlike either comp, every proposal here passes an independent Governor with three permanent HARD checks (student-verified, effect-must-be-propose, scope-exclusion) and safety-concern flags ALWAYS escalate to a human, never auto-commit at any rollout phase -- neither SchoolCues nor Bloomz structurally enforces anything comparable. This band is DELIBERATELY NOT the ¥50k-150k/月 portfolio-uniform range used by 6399/6310/7810/5820 -- that range was anchored on HR/recruiting/CRM per-seat SaaS competitors, which have no evidenced relationship to K-12 school administrative-coordination pricing; applying it here without evidence would be exactly the kind of unfounded number this ledger exists to prevent. Managed Starter opened at ¥25,000/月 flat, per school." :rec/run-id "pricing-intel-20260722-01" :rec/at "2026-07-22" :rec/seq 142}
{:rec/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-852] :rec/band-low 15000.0 :rec/band-high 40000.0 :rec/unit "¥/school/月 (flat, unlimited seats)" :rec/rationale "Reuses isic-851's pricing-intel-20260722-01 competitor research (obs seq 137-141) verbatim rather than re-surveying: secondary schools buy the same category of K-12 communication/coordination software as primary schools (SchoolCues, Bloomz, ParentSquare, Brightwheel, Procare), just a different grade band -- no evidence exists that pricing differs by grade band within K-12. Same band and same Managed Starter price (¥25,000/月) as isic-851." :rec/run-id "pricing-intel-20260723-01" :rec/at "2026-07-23" :rec/seq 143}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-853] :obs/product [:product/id :product/waitwell] :obs/price-summary "Queue/appointment management for advising and service desks: Starter tier published at $29/mo per location, includes advising booking, queue management, and check-in" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/published :obs/source-url "https://waitwellsoftware.com/resources/articles/best-enrollment-management-software-higher-education/" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260723-01" :obs/at "2026-07-23" :obs/seq 144}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-853] :obs/product [:product/id :product/supersaas] :obs/price-summary "General-purpose appointment scheduling (not higher-ed-specific): published starting price $9/mo, scales from small schools to large universities" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/published :obs/source-url "https://www.supersaas.com/info/schools-and-universities-appointment-planning" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260723-01" :obs/at "2026-07-23" :obs/seq 145}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-853] :obs/product [:product/id :product/slate] :obs/price-summary "Full admissions/enrollment-management CRM (a different product category than back-office coordination -- included only to show the market's price ceiling): starts at $30,000/year for smaller institutions, per a third-party comparison; institution-wide enterprise pricing, not self-serve" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/estimated :obs/source-url "https://waitwellsoftware.com/resources/articles/best-enrollment-management-software-higher-education/" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260723-01" :obs/at "2026-07-23" :obs/seq 146}
{:rec/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-853] :rec/band-low 8000.0 :rec/band-high 25000.0 :rec/unit "¥/department-or-institution/月 (flat, unlimited seats)" :rec/rationale "Higher-ed's own enterprise student-success platforms (Starfish/EAB Navigate, Symplicity) are institution-wide and sales-gated with zero public pricing, consistent with the sales-gated pattern found in K-12 (ParentSquare/Brightwheel/Procare). Two narrower scheduling-only tools DO publish pricing -- WaitWell $29/mo/location and SuperSaaS from $9/mo -- both well below K-12's SchoolCues/Bloomz anchors (~¥1,350-4,350/月 converted at ~¥150/$). Slate (a full admissions CRM, different category) starts at $30,000/year for smaller institutions, cited only to show the market's real spread, not as a direct comparable. This actor's scope sits above the bare-scheduling tools (governed audit ledger, supply/staffing coordination, permanent safety/scope-exclusion blocks none of them ship) but nowhere near enterprise-CRM territory. ¥20,000/月 lands just above the WaitWell/SuperSaaS converted range to reflect that added governance value. Deliberately NOT the ¥50,000-150,000/月 portfolio-uniform range the HR/CRM/recruiting flagships use -- this market's own real comps price meaningfully lower than either K-12 or that unrelated SaaS cluster. Managed Advising Ops (Starter) opened at ¥20,000/月 flat, per department/institution." :rec/run-id "pricing-intel-20260723-01" :rec/at "2026-07-23" :rec/seq 147}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-854] :obs/product [:product/id :product/talentlms] :obs/price-summary "LMS/course-content platform (different problem than back-office coordination): Core plan $149/mo flat for up to 100 users (annual billing ~$119/mo); Grow $299/mo, Pro $579/mo; Enterprise custom; free tier up to 5 users/10 courses" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/published :obs/source-url "https://research.com/software/reviews/talentlms-review" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260723-01" :obs/at "2026-07-23" :obs/seq 148}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-854] :obs/product [:product/id :product/trainual] :obs/price-summary "Employee training/SOP documentation platform (different problem again): historically $3-5/user/mo, but no longer publishes self-serve pricing -- final cost now determined during a sales process based on team size and features" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/estimated :obs/source-url "https://www.educate-me.co/blog/trainual-pricing" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260723-01" :obs/at "2026-07-23" :obs/seq 149}
{:obs/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-854] :obs/product [:product/id :product/coursebox] :obs/price-summary "AI course-authoring/LMS platform (different problem again): Creator $30/mo (unlimited courses/learners); Pro $150 first month then $300/mo; Business $700/mo (10 admin licenses, API access)" :obs/disclosure-tier :tier/published :obs/source-url "https://www.coursebox.ai/pricing" :obs/run-id "pricing-intel-20260723-01" :obs/at "2026-07-23" :obs/seq 150}
{:rec/vertical [:vertical/id :vertical/isic-854] :rec/band-low 12000.0 :rec/band-high 30000.0 :rec/unit "¥/provider/月 (flat, unlimited seats)" :rec/rationale "No exact 'back-office coordination for a training provider' comparable exists publicly, so this is anchored against the nearest real comparables a training provider already budgets for -- TalentLMS Core $149/mo, Trainual $3-5/user/mo (now sales-gated), Coursebox $30-700/mo -- while being explicit that NONE of them solve the same problem (course content/delivery, not scheduling/facility/staffing coordination); a real provider would still need something like this actor IN ADDITION to whichever of those it uses, not instead of it. ¥20,000/月 (~$130/mo at ~¥150/$) sits in the lower-middle of that converted spread, reflecting that this is a narrower single-purpose coordination tool. Deliberately NOT the ¥50,000-150,000/月 portfolio-uniform range the HR/CRM/recruiting flagships use, which this market's own (admittedly imperfect) comps don't support either. Managed Training Ops (Starter) opened at ¥20,000/月 flat, per provider." :rec/run-id "pricing-intel-20260723-01" :rec/at "2026-07-23" :rec/seq 151}

